<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lithuanian Metrica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lithuanian Metrica is the archive of the chancery of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, consisting of copybooks of charters, court decisions, treaties and other records from the fifteenth to the eighteenth century. Most entries are in Ruthenian, with later ones in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> and Polish. Taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> after the partitions, most of it is now held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and it is a major source for the history of the grand duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lithuanian-metrica.jpg" alt="Lithuanian Metrica" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Metryka_litewska.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
